    "updated_at": "2024-10-21T23:55:30Z",
    "body": "> I wonder if it would be less cognitive overhead for authors and more forwards compatible if ElementInternals instead provided a way to specify when a control has been interacted with. \r\n\r\nYes. I’m currently tracking my own interaction heuristics for FACEs, so this would be very helpful.\r\n\r\nThis is probably out of scope for the current discussion, but a way to offload the heuristics to native form controls would be helpful as well. Perhaps a `userinteracted` event or something like that.",
