    "created_at": "2025-03-17T15:04:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-17T15:06:20Z",
    "body": "I'm currently using my own ad-hoc solution to ignore the internal error state if the user has not interacted with a form:\n\n```js\n  erroredState({ error, _invalid, _userInteracted }) { return _userInteracted && Boolean(error || _invalid); },\n```\n```js\n    .events({\n      blur() {\n        this._userInteracted = true;\n        this.checkValidity();\n      },\n    })\n```\n```js\n      formResetCallback() {\n        this._formReset = true; // Fires Change Event\n        this._valueDirty = false;\n        this.checkValidity();\n        this._userInteracted = false; // Reset error states\n        this._formReset = false;\n      },\n```\n\nIIRC, I used the `blur` setup because informing a user of an error while they're still typing (eg: password not minimum length) is not user friendly.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
